{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01L1", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-immersions-monomorphisms}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:478e01b3aeb7c169210106fcb3264de48799a4b14ad8370e616f3226520ffd07", "source_text": "An immersion of schemes is a monomorphism.\nIn particular, any immersion is separated.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:acd2a5e330a84ac3f64a946a9a96cf1cef9c0f3c0d9f544a864889674d3df109", "unit_id": "tag:01L7:statement"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01L1", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-injective-points-surjective-stalks}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-restrict-map-to-opens}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-characterize-closed-subspace}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:15bda1724072da8381c7d6a17bfaf8d14d61b0615a47709204a3d71cd4f90435", "source_text": "We can see this by checking that the criterion of\nLemma <REF_0001> applies.\nMore elegantly perhaps, we can use that\nLemmas <REF_0002> and\n<REF_0003> imply that\nopen and closed immersions are monomorphisms and hence\nany immersion (which is a composition of such)\nis a monomorphism.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0a02cd286e1dd026abe311a0e978935feb9b49f25fe1fbe652ce03e517420af7", "unit_id": "tag:01L7:proof"}
